1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Chinese saw — a Forbidden
City in the sky.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
The whole sky turns around one place:
here.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The palace of the Sky Emperor. Beijing’s
Forbidden City is named after it.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Two walls, left and right, wrap around
it like arms.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The five Pole stars. One of them is
called Di: “the Emperor.”

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Today’s Pole Star was not the ancient
emperor’s star.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
3,000 years ago, the Sky Emperor lived
in Di: the star Kochab.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Earth’s axis slowly wobbles, once in
26,000 years. The Emperor has moved
house.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Outside the palace, two more cities.
First, in the spring sky: the
government.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
At its heart sit the Thrones of the Five
Emperors.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Their first star is Leo’s tail,
Denebola. One star: a lion’s tail and an
emperor’s seat.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The third city is the busiest: a market.
Even the Sky Emperor goes shopping.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Add the 28 mansions around them: a human
world, projected onto the sky.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:23,000
All three are up: the palace in the
north, the government high in the south,
the market rising in the east.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Australia: an emu made of darkness.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

